The behaviour in qemu-2.10 is nearly the same as in qemu-2.9. The only
difference is a different kind of crash for m68k:

$ QEMU_LD_PREFIX=3D/usr/m68k-linux-gnu QEMU_CPU=3Dm68020 ~/inst-qemu/2.9.0/=
bin/qemu-m68k hello.m68k
qemu: uncaught target signal 4 (Illegal instruction) - core dumped

$ QEMU_LD_PREFIX=3D/usr/m68k-linux-gnu QEMU_CPU=3Dm68020 ~/inst-qemu/2.10.0=
/bin/qemu-m68k hello.m68k
qemu: uncaught target signal 11 (Segmentation fault) - core dumped

